+/**
+ * @file network_coordinator.cpp Client for the OpenTTD Game Coordinator.
+ *
+ * Replaces the dead-in-practice UDP master server. master.openttd.org does still
+ * answer, but every address it hands back belongs to a modern server that no longer
+ * listens on UDP at all, so the old path can only ever produce blank list entries.
+ *
+ * This implementation deliberately does NOT use the Packet class: Packet embeds a
+ * fixed byte[SEND_MTU] (1460) buffer, while a single GC_LISTING packet reaches over
+ * 3 KB. Raising SEND_MTU globally would change how the game protocol chunks the map
+ * transfer and would put 32 KB on every queued packet on a 24 MB machine, so this
+ * socket gets its own heap buffers and its own little-endian primitives instead.
+ *
+ * Wire details, and why we announce protocol version 2, are in core/tcp_coordinator.h.
+ */
